@prefix backlog: <http://example.org/backlog#> .
@prefix ex: <http://example.org/proposal#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

# Draft delivery lineage exported by the Proposal Workbench (BRSF software-development profile). Refine, then validate with the BRSF validator.

ex:Mission a backlog:Mission ; rdfs:label "ShopTrack: Python Inventory and Sales Tracker for a Small Shop in Taif"@en ; backlog:hasMissionStatement "ShopTrack gives the shop owner and shop staff of a small shop in Taif a simple Python web application to record sales, see live stock levels and receive low-stock alerts, so the shop owner stops losing sales to empty shelves and spends minutes, not hours, on weekly stock and sales reports." ; backlog:hasMissionOutcome "Once ShopTrack exists, the shop owner opens one page and sees what is in stock, what sold this week and which products must be reordered today. Shop staff record a sale in a few taps on a phone, and the stock updates automatically, which the Excel sheets and notebook can never do." ; backlog:hasIntentOrigin backlog:IOrigin_Derived .
ex:Lineage a backlog:Lineage ; backlog:lineageForMission ex:Mission ; backlog:adoptsObligationSet backlog:OS_SDLC_v2 .
ex:Customer1 a backlog:Stakeholder ; rdfs:label "The Koozie Corner, Taif, Saudi Arabia"@en ; rdfs:comment "Customer (owner): One simple web tool that replaces their Excel sheets and notebook: live stock, weekly sales and low-stock alerts in one place."@en .
ex:EndUser1 a backlog:Stakeholder ; rdfs:label "Shop owner"@en ; rdfs:comment "End user: The owner who runs the shop and orders from suppliers - Checks stock, sees weekly sales reports and decides what to reorder (daily, Laptop or phone browser)"@en .
ex:EndUser2 a backlog:Stakeholder ; rdfs:label "Shop staff"@en ; rdfs:comment "End user: Cashiers and helpers working at the shop counter - Record each sale and register new stock when deliveries arrive (daily, Phone or tablet browser at the counter)"@en .
ex:Scope a backlog:ScopeStatement ; backlog:scopeForMission ex:Mission ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage ; backlog:coversArea ex:A1, ex:A2, ex:A3, ex:A4 ; backlog:requiresDeliverable ex:D1, ex:D2, ex:D3, ex:D4, ex:D5, ex:D6, ex:D7 ; backlog:hasScopeExclusion ex:X1, ex:X2, ex:X3, ex:X4 .
ex:A1 a backlog:ScopeArea ; rdfs:label "Product and stock management"@en ; backlog:areaLocation "Flask web app, products and stock tables in SQLite" ; backlog:areaMeasure "Excel sheets and a paper notebook that often do not match" .
ex:A2 a backlog:ScopeArea ; rdfs:label "Sales recording"@en ; backlog:areaLocation "Sales page used by shop staff at the counter" ; backlog:areaMeasure "Sales noted in a notebook, copied into Excel later" .
ex:A3 a backlog:ScopeArea ; rdfs:label "Reports and alerts"@en ; backlog:areaLocation "Dashboard page with charts and alerts" ; backlog:areaMeasure "No reports; weekly totals added up by hand" .
ex:A4 a backlog:ScopeArea ; rdfs:label "Data import, validation and export"@en ; backlog:areaLocation "CSV import tool, SHACL validation, CSV and JSON-LD export" ; backlog:areaMeasure "No machine-readable data" .
ex:D1 a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ; rdfs:label "Product list with add, edit, delete and stock-in"@en ; backlog:deliverableForArea ex:A1 ; backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Product ; backlog:hasProductScopeKind backlog:Kind_Functional .
ex:D2 a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ; rdfs:label "Stock can never go below zero; every change is recorded"@en ; backlog:deliverableForArea ex:A1 ; backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Product ; backlog:hasProductScopeKind backlog:Kind_NonFunctional .
ex:D3 a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ; rdfs:label "Sales page that records a sale and reduces stock"@en ; backlog:deliverableForArea ex:A2 ; backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Product ; backlog:hasProductScopeKind backlog:Kind_Functional .
ex:D4 a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ; rdfs:label "Recording a sale takes under 15 seconds on a phone"@en ; backlog:deliverableForArea ex:A2 ; backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Product ; backlog:hasProductScopeKind backlog:Kind_NonFunctional .
ex:D5 a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ; rdfs:label "Dashboard with weekly sales chart, best sellers and low-stock alerts"@en ; backlog:deliverableForArea ex:A3 ; backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Product ; backlog:hasProductScopeKind backlog:Kind_Functional .
ex:D6 a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ; rdfs:label "CSV import with validation and error report; CSV and JSON-LD export"@en ; backlog:deliverableForArea ex:A4 ; backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Product ; backlog:hasProductScopeKind backlog:Kind_Functional .
ex:D7 a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ; rdfs:label "Unit tests with pytest and a short user guide for the shop"@en ; backlog:deliverableForArea ex:A4 ; backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Work ; backlog:hasProductScopeKind backlog:Kind_NonFunctional .
ex:X1 a backlog:ScopeExclusion ; rdfs:label "Card payments and a cash-register (POS) integration"@en ; backlog:hasExclusionRationale "Payment systems need certification and bank contracts; the shop keeps its existing payment method." .
ex:X2 a backlog:ScopeExclusion ; rdfs:label "E-invoicing (ZATCA Fatoora) and VAT accounting"@en ; backlog:hasExclusionRationale "Official Saudi tax invoices need an approved e-invoicing solution and an accountant; out of reach in one term." .
ex:X3 a backlog:ScopeExclusion ; rdfs:label "Online shop for customers"@en ; backlog:hasExclusionRationale "The problem is inside the shop (stock and sales); selling online is a different project." .
ex:X4 a backlog:ScopeExclusion ; rdfs:label "Customer personal data and loyalty cards"@en ; backlog:hasExclusionRationale "Not needed to solve the stock problem and would bring personal-data obligations." .
ex:G1 a backlog:Goal ; rdfs:label "The shop owner always knows what is in stock and what to reorder, without counting shelves"@en ; backlog:derivesFromScope ex:Scope ; backlog:contributesToMission ex:Mission ; backlog:hasGoalFacing backlog:Facing_Mission ; backlog:goalCoversArea ex:A3 ; backlog:hasGoalRationale "This is the change the mission promises." .
ex:G2 a backlog:Goal ; rdfs:label "Products, sales, reports and data import all work together in one delivered application"@en ; backlog:derivesFromScope ex:Scope ; backlog:contributesToMission ex:Mission ; backlog:hasGoalFacing backlog:Facing_Scope ; backlog:goalCoversArea ex:A1 ; backlog:hasGoalRationale "Every scope area must be finished, not only the easy part." .
ex:G3 a backlog:Goal ; rdfs:label "Sales recording stays simple: no payments, invoices or online shop"@en ; backlog:derivesFromScope ex:Scope ; backlog:contributesToMission ex:Mission ; backlog:hasGoalFacing backlog:Facing_Containment ; backlog:goalCoversArea ex:A2 ; backlog:hasGoalRationale "Keeps effort inside the named areas so the project fits one term." .
ex:G4 a backlog:Goal ; rdfs:label "Only valid product data ever enters the database"@en ; backlog:derivesFromScope ex:Scope ; backlog:contributesToMission ex:Mission ; backlog:hasGoalFacing backlog:Facing_Scope ; backlog:goalCoversArea ex:A4 ; backlog:hasGoalRationale "Wrong imported data would make every stock figure and report wrong." .
ex:Spec a backlog:Specification ; backlog:hasSpecificationText "The shop owner signs in and imports the existing product list from a CSV file; each row is checked against a SHACL shape and invalid rows are listed with the reason. Owner and staff can add and edit products and register stock arriving from suppliers. Staff record a sale by choosing products and quantities; the system saves the sale, reduces the stock of each product and refuses a sale larger than the stock. When a product's stock falls to its reorder level, it appears in the low-stock alert list. The dashboard shows this week's sales total, a daily sales chart and the best-selling products. The owner can export products and sales as CSV or JSON-LD." .
ex:Scen1 a backlog:TestScenario ; backlog:scenarioOf ex:Spec ; backlog:scenarioKind backlog:Scen_Nominal ; backlog:hasScenarioText "Given a product with 10 in stock, when staff record a sale of 3, then the sale is saved and the stock shows 7." .
ex:Scen2 a backlog:TestScenario ; backlog:scenarioOf ex:Spec ; backlog:scenarioKind backlog:Scen_Rejection ; backlog:hasScenarioText "Given a product with 2 in stock, when staff try to record a sale of 5, then the sale is refused with the message Not enough stock and nothing changes." .
ex:Scen3 a backlog:TestScenario ; backlog:scenarioOf ex:Spec ; backlog:scenarioKind backlog:Scen_Rejection ; backlog:hasScenarioText "Given a CSV row with a negative price, when the owner imports the file, then that row is rejected and shown in the error report with its line number." .
ex:Scen4 a backlog:TestScenario ; backlog:scenarioOf ex:Spec ; backlog:scenarioKind backlog:Scen_Boundary ; backlog:hasScenarioText "Given a product with reorder level 5 and stock 6, when one unit is sold, then the product appears in the low-stock alerts." .
ex:Scen5 a backlog:TestScenario ; backlog:scenarioOf ex:Spec ; backlog:scenarioKind backlog:Scen_Absent ; backlog:hasScenarioText "Given no sales recorded this week, when the owner opens the dashboard, then it shows zero sales and a clear empty-state message instead of an error." .
ex:O1 a backlog:Objective ; rdfs:label "Weekly time the owner spends counting stock and checking records"@en ; backlog:contributesToGoal ex:G1 ; backlog:hasMeasurementKind backlog:Meas_Judged ; backlog:hasMeasurementQuery "Owner's own estimate in hours per week, asked on 17 Oct 2026 and again after 2 weeks of use" ; backlog:hasBaselineValue "4-5 hours per week (owner's answer, 17 Oct 2026)" ; backlog:hasTargetValue "under 1 hour" ; backlog:hasTargetDirection backlog:Dir_Decrease .
ex:O2 a backlog:Objective ; rdfs:label "Share of planned test cases that pass"@en ; backlog:contributesToGoal ex:G2 ; backlog:hasMeasurementKind backlog:Meas_Derived ; backlog:hasMeasurementQuery "Passed pytest cases divided by planned test cases, from the test report" ; backlog:hasBaselineValue "0%" ; backlog:hasTargetValue "at least 90%" ; backlog:hasTargetDirection backlog:Dir_Increase .
ex:O3 a backlog:Objective ; rdfs:label "Work items outside the four scope areas"@en ; backlog:contributesToGoal ex:G3 ; backlog:hasMeasurementKind backlog:Meas_Counted ; backlog:hasMeasurementQuery "Count of commits or log entries not linked to a story of epics E1-E4" ; backlog:hasBaselineValue "0" ; backlog:hasTargetValue "0" ; backlog:hasTargetDirection backlog:Dir_Hold .
ex:O4 a backlog:Objective ; rdfs:label "Invalid product rows that reach the database"@en ; backlog:contributesToGoal ex:G4 ; backlog:hasMeasurementKind backlog:Meas_Counted ; backlog:hasMeasurementQuery "Import a test CSV with 20 known-bad rows; count how many are stored" ; backlog:hasBaselineValue "No validation" ; backlog:hasTargetValue "0" ; backlog:hasTargetDirection backlog:Dir_Hold .
ex:Model_Activity a backlog:ModelArtifact ; backlog:hasModelKind backlog:Kind_ActivityDiagram ; backlog:hasModelLevel backlog:Level_Analysis ; backlog:declaresState "Recording a sale: 1. Staff opens the sales page. 2. Searches or scans a product and enters the quantity. 3. System checks stock: if the quantity is larger than the stock, show Not enough stock and return to step 2; otherwise continue. 4. Staff confirms the sale. 5. System saves the sale and a stock movement and reduces stock. 6. If the new stock is at or below the reorder level, add the product to the low-stock alerts. 7. Show the sale receipt on screen. Import branch: owner uploads CSV, each row is validated, valid rows are saved, invalid rows go to the error report." .
ex:Model_Sequence a backlog:ModelArtifact ; backlog:hasModelKind backlog:Kind_SequenceDiagram ; backlog:hasModelLevel backlog:Level_Analysis ; backlog:declaresState "Staff -> Sales page: choose product and quantity. Sales page -> Flask route /sales: POST sale. Route -> SaleService: record_sale(items). SaleService -> Product repository: get stock. Product repository -> SaleService: current stock. SaleService -> Database: save Sale and StockMovement, update stock (one transaction). SaleService -> AlertService: check_reorder(product). AlertService -> SaleService: alert or none. SaleService -> Route: result. Route -> Staff: confirmation page with new stock." .
ex:Model_Class a backlog:ModelArtifact ; backlog:hasModelKind backlog:Kind_ClassDiagram ; backlog:hasModelLevel backlog:Level_Analysis ; backlog:declaresState "Product (id, name, category, barcode, price, stock, reorder_level; methods: add_stock(qty), remove_stock(qty), needs_reorder()). StockMovement (id, product, quantity, kind: IN | SALE | CORRECTION, time). Sale (id, time, user, total; has 1..* SaleItem). SaleItem (product, quantity, unit_price). User (id, name, role: OWNER | STAFF, password_hash). Services: SaleService (record_sale), ImportService (import_csv, validate_row), ReportService (weekly_total, best_sellers, low_stock). Product 1 -- 0..* StockMovement; Sale 1 -- 1..* SaleItem; SaleItem * -- 1 Product." .
ex:Backlog a backlog:Backlog ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage ; backlog:appliesDefinitionOfDone ex:DoD .
